# Kavacha patch 0051 — named container sharing across Spaces, and editing an
# existing Space's description (REMAINING_WORK.md §3 "Workspaces / identity").
#
# CONTAINER SHARING. Patch 0038 made per-Space containers opt-in; what it did
# not give anyone is a way to say "these three Spaces are all me at work".
# Mechanically that was always possible — Zen's space actions menu already
# routed through contextChangeContainerTab, which writes workspace.containerTabId
# — but the menu was Firefox's generic createUserContextMenu, labelled "Default
# profile", and it HID the container the Space was already in. So the one fact
# that matters for sharing (which Spaces are in which container) was the one
# fact the UI refused to show. Kavacha builds the menu itself now: every public
# container, radio-checked on the current one, labelled with how many OTHER
# Spaces share it; "No container" as the shared-sign-ins default; and "New
# container…", which is why hide-if-usercontext-disabled had to go — with no
# containers yet, an empty hidden menu is a dead end.
#
# THE MIGRATION GOTCHA, which REMAINING_WORK asked for by name: containers are
# separate FIRST-PARTY cookie jars, so moving a Space between them does not
# carry its cookies. Every site the user was signed into in that Space reads as
# signed out. It is fully recoverable — the cookies are still in the old
# container, and switching back restores them — but it is silent and it looks
# exactly like data loss, so the switch now goes through a confirm that names
# the container being left. Nothing is deleted either way; this is a warning,
# not a guard.
#
# DESCRIPTION. Patch 0014 captured a Space description in the creation card and
# stored it on the space object — and nothing in the browser ever read it back.
# It was write-once and invisible, which is why "edit it" stayed open. Two
# halves land together, because either alone is pointless: an "Edit Description…"
# item in the space actions menu (prefilled, blank DELETES the key rather than
# storing "", matching 0014's rule so it never rides sync empty), and the Space
# strip button's tooltip as the place it is finally shown.
#
# Why a patch: the menus live in Zen's popupset and the handlers are methods on
# nsZenWorkspaces; the container submenu's population and command handler are
# both upstream Zen code being replaced, not extended.
#
# Touches: src/zen/spaces/ZenSpaceManager.mjs (menu builder, confirm, create,
#          description editor), src/zen/spaces/ZenSpaceIcons.mjs (tooltip),
#          src/browser/base/content/zen-panels/popups.inc (menu items),
#          locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-workspaces.ftl (strings).
# Applies on top of 0050.
